// rk_swing_ui_padfx_side.jsfx-inc
// Swing: the SIDE SLOT -- the pad editor, the step sequencer (when placed at the side) and the mini browser (when not
// placed below) in the column right of the pads, side by side when the slot has the room (the render), as tabs when it
// has not -- and its dispatcher. Round two J (2026-10-22; the user: "build the per pad fx inside swing from our render"
// / "where both the browser and pad fx are visible" / "FX and Sound should be in the same tab" / "build the swap: the
// sequencer at the side and the browser at the bottom as options"). The renders: mockups/Swing_Seq_View_option4a.png
// (the editor and the browser beside the pads), _sideways.png (the sequencer at the side); the rule: Spec_Swing_Seq_View
// 7.1 (placements; two panels in one slot: side by side when the screen has the room, tabs until it does).
// (c) EON Studios — All Rights Reserved
//
// HOW IT HANGS TOGETHER
//   * The slot is the mini browser's column (rk_swing_ui_minibrowser): its gate claims the column's mouse, asks the bridge
//     for width and squeezes the pads where the window cannot grow. The gate reads swing_side_open() / swing_side_want_w()
//     (defined there): the panels PLACED at the side and open -- the browser unless fb_place is BELOW (3), the editor, the
//     sequencer when seq_place is RIGHT (1) -- and the SUM of their widths (the browser's 292 + its rail, the editor's 420,
//     the sequencer's SEQ_SIDE_W 600). The bottom slot is the sequencer's gate (rk_seq_ui swing_seq_gate / under_draw):
//     the sequencer unless placed at the side, the browser when placed below.
//   * swing_side_draw replaces swing_fb_draw at the host's two draw sites. Closed: the browser's draw alone (its gutter and
//     chevron). Open: a 22 px row across the top, then the panels. SIDE BY SIDE (pfx_split: two or more of the open panels
//     fit the slot): the columns left to right -- the editor, the sequencer, the browser with the gutter -- each taking the
//     presses in its own column from the gate's stash; the top row shows their titles. Which open panels show
//     (swing_side_fit; the owner, 2026-10-27: "show as many side by side as fit and stack only the rest as tabs"): the
//     front panel (side_front: 0 the browser, 1 the editor, 2 the sequencer -- the one picked last) always, then the one in
//     front before it (side_prev, kept for the session only: a load starts it at -1, the rest in column order), then the
//     rest in column order, each while the sum of their MINIMUM widths still fits (2026-10-27, "squeeze before tabbing":
//     the shown ones then share the room, each growing back from its minimum toward its own width in proportion to what
//     it gave up); they draw in COLUMN order whatever the pick order, the rest of the width past their own widths going
//     to the last shown column. An open panel left out keeps a TAB cell in the top row at its place in
//     column order (a press brings it to the front; the least recently picked shown panel becomes the tab). All of them
//     fitting is the old rule's own test, so that case draws as before. TABS when only the front fits: the front panel
//     alone under the tabs; the browser in front draws as ever; another panel in front (or the browser left out beside
//     two others): the browser's draw still runs (it owns the gutter, its chevron and its state) but BLIND -- the mouse
//     parked off-canvas, the stash and the frame's key emptied for the call -- and the panels paint over its body. A
//     browser placed BELOW (fb_place 3) is never drawn here: the slot paints its own gutter instead
//     (swing_side_gutter_draw) -- a blind call would still advance the browser's press and release shadows and its
//     keyboard flags, and the live browser below missed its drop and lost the filter's focus (the swap's audit).
//   * The gutter's handle FOLDS the whole slot in every mode; each panel's X (in its title cell) closes that panel alone.
//     The SEAM between the pads and the slot (FB_SEAM_W, part of the slot's width while open) is the slot's WIDTH HANDLE
//     (swing_side_seam_draw paints it; swing_side_handle in the browser lib reads it: drag, wheel, right-click = the
//     panels' own widths; the dragged width's rest goes to the last open column).
//     Nothing open at the side and the browser placed below: the handle opens the panel placed at the side (the
//     sequencer when it is, else the pad editor). Side by side, a present panel that is closed keeps a narrow dim cell
//     in the title row, so it can be opened without folding the others.
//   * The editor's content IS the pad editor, whole and in the editor's own order (rk_swing_ui_grid_overlay / _fx sections,
//     handed the column through the editor's globals and put back after); the sequencer's IS its panel draw
//     (swing_seq_panel_draw, rectangle-fed: its toolbar, chips and footer already fold for a narrow width), with the gate's
//     stashed mouse handed in and the keys served here while it is at the side. A modal up hands the sections no mouse;
//     while the pad editor itself is open over the pads the editor's column shows a note instead.
//   * pfx_open and side_front are saved with the project (gate 80); seq_place / fb_place / fx_place ride the sequencer's
//     SETTINGS block (cells 7 / 8 / 9, Spec 7.1), set from the sequencer's OPT menu; fb_h (the browser's height below)
//     under gate 81, fx_h (the editor's) and pfx_page under 82. The editor placed below (fx_place 3) is not present here:
//     the bottom slot draws its wide form (rk_swing_ui_padfx_panel) and the PAD FX button opens it there.
//   * Window and rack-face passes only, as the browser: an embed pass never reaches swing_side_draw.
@init

// which panels the side slot holds (present) and shows (open), by k: 0 the browser, 1 the editor, 2 the sequencer
function swing_side_present(k) ( k == 0 ? fb_place != 3 : k == 1 ? fx_place != 3 : seq_place == 1; );
function swing_side_isopen(k)  ( k == 0 ? (fb_open && fb_place != 3) : k == 1 ? (pfx_open && fx_place != 3) : (seq_shown && seq_place == 1); );
function swing_side_pw(k)      ( k == 0 ? FB_PANEL_W + (fb_tree ? swing_fb_tree_w() : 0) : k == 1 ? PFX_PANEL_W : SEQ_SIDE_W; );

// ── Which open panels show side by side (the owner, 2026-10-27: "show as many side by side as fit and stack only the rest
// as tabs"). All @gfx; nothing here is saved (pfx_open / side_front under gate 80 are the saved state, as before).
//   side_sh0 / 1 / 2: shown this frame, by k (swing_side_fit sets them; the columns and the top row read them)
//   side_prev: the panel in front just before side_front -- the fit's second pick; -1 = none known (a load, or a reload:
//              the rest go in column order). side_last: side_front as the slot last laid it out (the change is seen
//              there, whoever set side_front: a tab, the PAD FX / SEQ buttons, the OPT menu, the gutter).
side_sh0 = 0; side_sh1 = 0; side_sh2 = 0;
side_prev = -1; side_last = -1;
SIDE_TAB_CELL_B = 100;   // an open panel's TAB cell beside the columns, design px: its title and its X (a closed one's dim cell is 72)
function swing_side_shown(k) ( k == 0 ? side_sh0 : k == 1 ? side_sh1 : side_sh2; );
// SQUEEZE BEFORE TABBING (the owner, 2026-10-27): a panel may give up width down to its own minimum (PFX_SIDE_MIN_W,
// SEQ_SIDE_MIN_W, the browser's list floor + the rail's; rk_swing_ui_minibrowser says why each) before any becomes a tab.
// side_cw0 / 1 / 2: each shown column's width this frame, by k, before a dragged width's rest (swing_side_fit sets them).
side_cw0 = 0; side_cw1 = 0; side_cw2 = 0;
side_sq = 0;   // this frame's columns are squeezed (the top row's middle cell reads it)
function swing_side_mw(k) ( min(swing_side_pw(k), k == 0 ? FB_LIST_MIN + (fb_tree ? FB_TREE_MIN : 0) : k == 1 ? PFX_SIDE_MIN_W : SEQ_SIDE_MIN_W); );
function swing_side_cw(k) ( k == 0 ? side_cw0 : k == 1 ? side_cw1 : side_cw2; );
// room = the panels' width (the slot less the seam and the gutter); sum = the open panels' widths. All of them fitting is
// decided by the old all-or-nothing test itself, so that case lays out exactly as before. Otherwise: the front panel,
// then side_prev, then the rest in column order (the editor, the sequencer, the browser), each taken when it still fits
// beside those taken AT ITS MINIMUM (the same 2 px margin). The ones taken fitting at their own widths: those widths, as
// before; else each gets its minimum plus a share of what is left in proportion to what it gave up, so all of them grow
// back together and reach their own widths at once. Returns how many show.
function swing_side_fit(room, sum) local(_sf_i, _sf_k, _sf_s, _sf_n, _sf_m)
(
  side_sh0 = 0; side_sh1 = 0; side_sh2 = 0; side_sq = 0;
  side_cw0 = swing_side_pw(0); side_cw1 = swing_side_pw(1); side_cw2 = swing_side_pw(2);
  room >= sum - 2 ? (
    side_sh0 = swing_side_isopen(0); side_sh1 = swing_side_isopen(1); side_sh2 = swing_side_isopen(2);
  ) : (
    _sf_s = 0; _sf_i = 0;
    loop(5,
      _sf_k = _sf_i == 0 ? side_front : _sf_i == 1 ? side_prev : _sf_i == 2 ? 1 : _sf_i == 3 ? 2 : 0;
      _sf_k >= 0 && swing_side_isopen(_sf_k) && !swing_side_shown(_sf_k) && (_sf_i == 0 || room >= _sf_s + swing_side_mw(_sf_k) - 2) ? (
        _sf_k == 0 ? side_sh0 = 1 : _sf_k == 1 ? side_sh1 = 1 : side_sh2 = 1;
        _sf_s += swing_side_mw(_sf_k);
      );
      _sf_i += 1;
    );
    // the squeeze: two or more shown that do not fit at their own widths (the front alone is the tabs: the whole slot)
    _sf_n = (side_sh0 ? side_cw0 : 0) + (side_sh1 ? side_cw1 : 0) + (side_sh2 ? side_cw2 : 0);
    side_sh0 + side_sh1 + side_sh2 >= 2 && room < _sf_n - 2 ? (
      side_sq = 1;
      _sf_m = max(0, room - _sf_s) / (_sf_n - _sf_s);   // > 0 apart: room >= _sf_s - 2 and room < _sf_n - 2
      side_cw0 = floor(swing_side_mw(0) + (side_cw0 - swing_side_mw(0)) * _sf_m);
      side_cw1 = floor(swing_side_mw(1) + (side_cw1 - swing_side_mw(1)) * _sf_m);
      side_cw2 = floor(swing_side_mw(2) + (side_cw2 - swing_side_mw(2)) * _sf_m);
    );
  );
  side_sh0 + side_sh1 + side_sh2;
);

// The set of open panels the dragged width (side_w, gate 83) was made for: another set puts the panels' own widths
// back. -1 = not seen yet: the first draw after @init adopts whatever is open WITHOUT clearing side_w, so a saved width
// survives the project's reload (until 2026-10-26 the count started at 0, every reload read "another set" on its first
// frame and zeroed the width the save had just restored; sweep LIB118). @init runs before @serialize restores side_w.
side_n_prev = -1;
function swing_side_seen(n) (
  n != side_n_prev ? ( side_n_prev >= 0 ? side_w = 0; side_n_prev = n; );
);

// ── The slot's top row: a cell per present panel in column order (the editor, the sequencer, the browser). Side by side:
// the cells are the shown columns' titles, and a present panel not shown keeps a narrow cell at its place, taken off a
// shown neighbour's title: a closed one a dim cell (the audit: with the editor and the sequencer side by side the browser
// had no cell and its chevron was blind -- no way to open it short of folding), an open one with no room beside the
// others a TAB cell (swing_side_fit; the open look and its X; a press brings it to the front). Tabs: equal cells, the lit
// one in front, a dim one opens its panel and brings it to the front. Each open panel's X at its cell's right end closes
// that panel alone -- and leaves the front where it was (until 2026-10-27 a press on a tab's X also made it the front
// for the frame, and the front then fell to the fallback order, away from the panel the user was on). ──
function swing_side_tabs_draw(x, y, w, h, split)
local(_st_i, _st_k, _st_x, _st_cw, _st_n, _st_on, _st_lit, _st_hot, _st_edge, _st_tw, _st_th, _st_bw, _st_xx, _st_w0, _st_w1, _st_w2, _st_dim, _st_tab, _st_c, _st_f0)
(
  _st_edge = _fb_g_lmbdown;
  _st_f0 = side_front;
  gfx_set(_fb_gr * 0.62, _fb_gg * 0.62, _fb_gb * 0.62, 1); gfx_rect(x, y, w, h);
  rk_font(1, swing_fs(9), 'b');
  _st_bw = w - FB_GUTTER_W;
  _st_n = swing_side_present(0) + swing_side_present(1) + swing_side_present(2);
  pfx_x_cx = -1; pfx_x_cy = -1; pfx_bx_cx = -1; pfx_bx_cy = -1; pfx_sx_cx = -1; pfx_sx_cy = -1;
  pfx_tab_x = x; pfx_tab_y = y; pfx_tab_h = h; pfx_tab_w = (_st_bw / _st_n) | 0;
  _st_w0 = 0; _st_w1 = 0; _st_w2 = 0;
  split ? (
    // the shown columns' widths as title cells (the browser's the rest); a present panel not shown: a cell of its own --
    // dim when closed, a tab when open -- taken off the shown neighbour after it (the one before it when none follows)
    _st_w1 = swing_side_shown(1) ? swing_side_cw(1) : 0; _st_w2 = swing_side_shown(2) ? swing_side_cw(2) : 0;   // the columns' widths, squeezed or their own (swing_side_fit)
    _st_w0 = swing_side_shown(0) ? (_st_bw - _st_w1 - _st_w2) : 0;
    !swing_side_shown(0) ? ( _st_w2 > 0 ? _st_w2 = _st_bw - _st_w1 : _st_w1 = _st_bw; );   // no browser shown: the last shown column's cell takes a dragged width's rest
    _st_dim = swing_px(72); _st_tab = swing_px(SIDE_TAB_CELL_B);
    swing_side_present(1) && !swing_side_shown(1) ? ( _st_c = swing_side_isopen(1) ? _st_tab : _st_dim; _st_w1 = _st_c; _st_w2 > 0 ? _st_w2 -= _st_c : _st_w0 -= _st_c; );
    // (squeezed, the sequencer's cell between the editor and the browser comes off the wider of the two: off a browser at
    // its minimum the cell left its title no room -- at 1.5x none at all, the title and its X gone)
    swing_side_present(2) && !swing_side_shown(2) ? ( _st_c = swing_side_isopen(2) ? _st_tab : _st_dim; _st_w2 = _st_c; _st_w0 > 0 && !(side_sq && _st_w1 > _st_w0) ? _st_w0 -= _st_c : _st_w1 -= _st_c; );
    swing_side_present(0) && !swing_side_shown(0) ? ( _st_c = swing_side_isopen(0) ? _st_tab : _st_dim; _st_w0 = _st_c; _st_w2 > 0 ? _st_w2 -= _st_c : _st_w1 -= _st_c; );
  );
  _st_x = x; _st_i = 0;
  loop(3,
    _st_k = _st_i == 0 ? 1 : _st_i == 1 ? 2 : 0;   // the column order: the editor, the sequencer, the browser
    swing_side_present(_st_k) ? (
      _st_on  = swing_side_isopen(_st_k);
      // the cell's width: its column side by side (the browser's the rest; a closed panel's dim cell), an equal share as tabs
      _st_cw = split ? (_st_k == 0 ? _st_w0 : _st_k == 1 ? _st_w1 : _st_w2) : pfx_tab_w;
      _st_cw > 0 ? (
        _st_lit = _st_on && (split ? swing_side_shown(_st_k) : side_front == _st_k);   // side by side: every shown column's title; an open tab beside them is not lit
        _st_hot = mx >= _st_x && mx < _st_x + _st_cw && my >= y && my < y + h;
        // the SOUND / SYNTH page chips' look and press (swing_pfx_pages_draw; the bottom slot's chips have it too) --
        // the owner, 2026-10-27: "make the pad FX and browser tabs switch ... the way the sound and synth tabs do": the
        // panel shown is a blue chip, the others the ground's chip, the words white (dimmer for a closed panel); a
        // press on a chip not shown brings its panel up and marks the project, as a page pick does. (Until then: a
        // light cell with the LCD tabs' red underline.)
        _st_lit ? gfx_set(0.25, 0.47, 0.68, 1) : gfx_set(_fb_gr * 0.78, _fb_gg * 0.78, _fb_gb * 0.78, _st_hot ? 1 : 0.9);
        gfx_rect(_st_x + swing_px(2), y + 2, _st_cw - swing_px(4), h - 4);
        gfx_set(1, 1, 1, _st_lit ? 1 : (_st_on ? 0.7 : 0.45));
        _st_k == 1 ? (
          (sel_pad >= 0 && sel_pad < NUM_SLOTS) ? ( swing_pad_lbl(sel_pad | 0, #pfx_lbl); sprintf(#pfx_ttl, "PAD FX  %s  %s", #pfx_lbl, get_name_slot(sel_pad | 0)); ) : strcpy(#pfx_ttl, "PAD FX");
        ) : strcpy(#pfx_ttl, _st_k == 2 ? "SEQ" : "BROWSER");
        gfx_measurestr(#pfx_ttl, _st_tw, _st_th);
        _st_tw > _st_cw - swing_px(30) ? ( strcpy(#pfx_ttl, _st_k == 1 ? "PAD FX" : _st_k == 2 ? "SEQ" : "BROWSER"); gfx_measurestr(#pfx_ttl, _st_tw, _st_th); );
        gfx_x = _st_x + max(swing_px(6), (_st_cw - _st_tw) * 0.5); gfx_y = y + (h - _st_th) * 0.5; gfx_drawstr(#pfx_ttl);
        _st_hot ? swing_tooltip_check(1480 + _st_k, _st_k == 0 ? "The sample browser in the side panel. Click to open it or bring it up; the others sit beside it as far as the room goes."
                                               : _st_k == 1 ? "The pad editor in the side panel: the pad you clicked last. Click to open it or bring it up; the others sit beside it as far as the room goes."
                                                            : "The step sequencer, placed at the side (OPT). Click to open it or bring it up; the others sit beside it as far as the room goes.");
        _st_hot && _st_edge && !_st_lit ? (
          _st_k == 0 ? ( fb_open = 1; side_front = 0; swing_fb_request(0, 0, -1); )
          : _st_k == 1 ? ( pfx_open = 1; side_front = 1; fb_kbd = 0; fb_filt_focus = 0; )
                       : ( seq_shown = 1; side_front = 2; fb_kbd = 0; fb_filt_focus = 0; seq_ui_focus = 1; );
          mark_dirty();   // what is open and in front is saved (gate 80), as the page chips' pfx_page is
        );
        // the X: closes this panel alone
        _st_on ? (
          _st_xx = _st_x + _st_cw - swing_px(12);
          _st_hot = abs(mx - _st_xx) <= swing_px(8) && abs(my - (y + h * 0.5)) <= swing_px(8);
          gfx_set(1, 1, 1, _st_hot ? 1 : 0.6);
          gfx_line(_st_xx - 4, y + h * 0.5 - 4, _st_xx + 4, y + h * 0.5 + 4); gfx_line(_st_xx - 4, y + h * 0.5 + 4, _st_xx + 4, y + h * 0.5 - 4);
          _st_hot ? swing_tooltip_check(1485 + _st_k, _st_k == 0 ? "Close the browser's panel." : _st_k == 1 ? "Close the pad editor's panel (PAD FX opens it again)." : "Close the sequencer's panel (SEQ opens it again).");
          _st_hot && _st_edge ? ( _st_k == 0 ? fb_open = 0 : _st_k == 1 ? pfx_open = 0 : seq_shown = 0; side_front = _st_f0; );   // the cell's press above took the front: give it back
          _st_k == 0 ? ( pfx_bx_cx = _st_xx; pfx_bx_cy = y + h * 0.5; ) : _st_k == 1 ? ( pfx_x_cx = _st_xx; pfx_x_cy = y + h * 0.5; ) : ( pfx_sx_cx = _st_xx; pfx_sx_cy = y + h * 0.5; );
        );
        _st_x += _st_cw;
      );
    );
    _st_i += 1;
  );
);

// ── The editor's column: the pad editor whole, for the pad clicked last, in its narrow form (rk_swing_ui_padfx_panel;
// the wide form draws below the pads). (x, y, w, h) = the column under the top row. The mouse the gate stashed is
// handed to the editor's controls (the browser's gain knob does the same); a modal up hands them none.
function swing_pfx_draw(x, y, w, h) local(_pf_modal) (
  _pf_modal = _ui_modal_up;
  lmb_down = _pf_modal ? 0 : _fb_g_lmbdown; LMB = _pf_modal ? 0 : _fb_g_lmbclick; rmb_down = _pf_modal ? 0 : _fb_g_rmbdown;
  frame_wheel = _pf_modal ? 0 : _fb_g_wheel;
  swing_pfx_panel_draw(x, y, w, h, 0);   // the pages, narrow; spends them
);

// ── The sequencer's column (seq_place RIGHT): its panel draw with the gate's stashed mouse; a press in the column gives
// it the keys, which are served here while it is at the side (the bottom slot's draw serves them below). ──
function swing_sseq_draw(x, y, w, h)
local(_sq_modal)
(
  pfx_seq_x = x; pfx_seq_w = w;
  _sq_modal = _ui_modal_up;
  lmb_down = _sq_modal ? 0 : _fb_g_lmbdown; LMB = _sq_modal ? 0 : _fb_g_lmbclick; rmb_down = _sq_modal ? 0 : _fb_g_rmbdown;
  frame_wheel = _sq_modal ? 0 : _fb_g_wheel;
  lmb_down && mx >= x && mx < x + w && my >= y && my < y + h ? seq_ui_focus = 1;
  swing_seq_panel_draw(x, y, w, h, 0);
  seq_ui_focus && seq_shown && !is_embedded && !fb_filt_focus && pne_pad < 0 && !swing_popup_active && _char > 0 ? seq_ui_keys();
  lmb_down = 0; LMB = 0; rmb_down = 0; frame_wheel = 0;
);

// the browser's draw with nothing to act on: the mouse parked off-canvas, the stash and the frame's key emptied
function swing_side_fb_blind(x, y, w, h)
local(_bl_mx, _bl_my, _bl_rx, _bl_ry, _bl_l, _bl_c, _bl_r, _bl_rc, _bl_w, _bl_ch)
(
  _bl_mx = mx; _bl_my = my; _bl_rx = mouse_x; _bl_ry = mouse_y; _bl_ch = _char;
  _bl_l = _fb_g_lmbdown; _bl_c = _fb_g_lmbclick; _bl_r = _fb_g_rmbdown; _bl_rc = _fb_g_rmbclick; _bl_w = _fb_g_wheel;
  mx = -10000; my = -10000; mouse_x = -10000; mouse_y = -10000; _char = 0;
  _fb_g_lmbdown = 0; _fb_g_lmbclick = 0; _fb_g_rmbdown = 0; _fb_g_rmbclick = 0; _fb_g_wheel = 0;
  fb_filt_focus = 0;
  swing_fb_draw(x, y, w, h);
  mx = _bl_mx; my = _bl_my; mouse_x = _bl_rx; mouse_y = _bl_ry; _char = _bl_ch;
  _fb_g_lmbdown = _bl_l; _fb_g_lmbclick = _bl_c; _fb_g_rmbdown = _bl_r; _fb_g_rmbclick = _bl_rc; _fb_g_wheel = _bl_w;
  fb_kbd = 0;
);

// The slot's gutter when the browser is placed BELOW the pads (fb_place 3): the browser's draw does not run here at all --
// a blind call would still advance its press and release shadows (_fb_lmb_prev, fb_kbd_prev) and its keyboard flags, and
// the LIVE browser below then missed its drop (the release edge spent) and lost the filter's focus every frame (found in
// the swap's audit, 2026-10-22). The ground, the seam, the grip and the chevron are painted the browser's way; the
// chevron points the way the slot will move. Open: the handle's press is the fold (swing_side_draw). Closed (nothing
// at the side): the press opens the panel placed at the side -- the sequencer when it is, else the pad editor.
function swing_side_gutter_draw(x, y, w, h, open)
local(_gd_gx, _gd_hot, _gd_cx, _gd_cy, _gd_i)
(
  swing_fb_ground();
  _gd_gx = x + w - FB_GUTTER_W;
  _gd_hot = mx >= _gd_gx && mx < _gd_gx + FB_GUTTER_W && my >= y && my < y + h;
  swing_fb_gutter_paint(_gd_gx, y, h, _gd_hot, open);   // the browser's own gutter look (the redraw, P1a: one painter for both)
  _gd_hot ? swing_tooltip_check(1489, open ? "Fold the side panels." : seq_place == 1 ? "Open the step sequencer at the side (the browser is placed below: OPT)." : fx_place != 3 ? "Open the pad editor at the side (the browser is placed below: OPT)." : "The panels are placed below the pads (the sequencer's OPT menu).");
  !open && _gd_hot && _fb_g_lmbdown ? ( seq_place == 1 ? ( seq_shown = 1; side_front = 2; seq_ui_focus = 1; ) : fx_place != 3 ? ( pfx_open = 1; side_front = 1; ) : 0; );
);

// ── The seam between the pads and the side panel: the slot's WIDTH HANDLE (the user, 2026-10-22: "in between the pads and
// where the pad FX is"). A slim strip in the slot's ground colour with three dots at mid-height, lit under the mouse or
// while a drag runs; swing_side_handle (the browser lib) reads the drag, the wheel and the right-click on it. ──
function swing_side_seam_draw(x, y, w, h) local(_ss_hot, _ss_cy, _ss_i) (
  _ss_hot = (mx >= x && mx < x + w && my >= y && my < y + h) || side_gdrag || swing_side_seam_ext(mx, my);   // + its reach over the pads' margin (2026-10-27)
  gfx_set(_fb_gr * 0.55, _fb_gg * 0.55, _fb_gb * 0.55, 1); gfx_rect(x, y, w, h);
  gfx_set(0, 0, 0, 0.35); gfx_rect(x, y, 1, h);
  gfx_set(1, 1, 1, 0.06); gfx_rect(x + w - 1, y, 1, h);
  // under the mouse or dragging: the seam lifts and its edge against the pads lights in the house blue (the owner,
  // 2026-10-27: "hard to grab" -- the bottom handle's top edge lights the same way, rk_seq_ui swing_seq_under_draw)
  _ss_hot ? ( gfx_set(1, 1, 1, 0.12); gfx_rect(x, y, w, h); gfx_set(0.20, 0.62, 0.86, 0.95); gfx_rect(x, y, max(2, swing_px(2)), h); );
  _ss_cy = y + h * 0.5;
  gfx_set(_fb_tc, _fb_tc, _fb_tc, _ss_hot ? 0.9 : 0.4);
  _ss_i = -1; loop(3, gfx_circle(x + w * 0.5, _ss_cy + _ss_i * swing_px(7), swing_px(1.5), 1, 1); _ss_i += 1; );
);

// ── The side slot: what the host draws in place of swing_fb_draw (the full face and the rack face). ──
function swing_side_draw(x, y, w, h)
local(_sd_th, _sd_gx, _sd_sx, _sd_sw, _sd_fb0, _sd_sum, _sd_n, _sd_cx, _sd_cw, _sd_rest, _sd_k, _sd_i, _sd_front_ok, _sd_fold, _sd_ns)
(
  // the PAD FX button's request (rk_swing_ui_panels_controls), applied here -- after swing_fb_snapshot posted this frame's
  // width request -- so the slot's gate baselines the window BEFORE the bridge widens it (the chevron's own timing)
  // placed below (fx_place 3) the button opens the editor under the pads and brings it to the front there (its stamp:
  // the bottom slot shows the last opened), and closes it when it is the one shown
  pfx_req == 1 ? ( pfx_open = 1; fx_place == 3 ? pfx_bstamp = (bot_stamp += 1) : ( side_front = 1; fb_kbd = 0; fb_filt_focus = 0; ); )
  : pfx_req == 2 ? ( pfx_open = 0; fx_place != 3 ? side_front = 0; );
  pfx_req = 0;
  // the front panel is always an open, present one: the one asked for, else the one in front before it (2026-10-27: the
  // front closed, the panel the user was on before it comes up), else the sequencer, the editor, the browser
  _sd_front_ok = swing_side_present(side_front) && swing_side_isopen(side_front);
  !_sd_front_ok ? ( side_front = ((side_prev >= 0 && swing_side_isopen(side_prev)) ? side_prev : (swing_side_isopen(2) ? 2 : (swing_side_isopen(1) ? 1 : 0))); );
  pfx_split = 0; pfx_seq_x = 0; pfx_seq_w = 0; side_sh0 = 0; side_sh1 = 0; side_sh2 = 0;
  _sd_n = swing_side_isopen(0) + swing_side_isopen(1) + swing_side_isopen(2);
  swing_side_seen(_sd_n);   // another set of panels: their own widths again (the handle's width was for the last set)
  // the front's history, whoever changed side_front (a tab, the PAD FX / SEQ buttons, the OPT menu, the gutter, a close):
  // the one it replaced is the one before it -- the fit's second pick. Not while nothing is open (a fold keeps it).
  _sd_n > 0 && side_front != side_last ? ( side_prev = side_last; side_last = side_front; );
  _sd_n == 0 ? (
    fb_place == 3 ? swing_side_gutter_draw(x, y, w, h, 0) : swing_fb_draw(x, y, w, h);   // placed below: the slot's own gutter (its press opens the panel placed here)
  ) : (
    _sd_th = swing_px(SIDE_TAB_H);
    _sd_sx = x + swing_px(FB_SEAM_W); _sd_sw = w - swing_px(FB_SEAM_W);   // the seam at the slot's left edge; the rest is the panels' and the gutter
    _sd_gx = x + w - FB_GUTTER_W;
    _sd_sum = (swing_side_isopen(0) ? swing_side_pw(0) : 0) + (swing_side_isopen(1) ? swing_side_pw(1) : 0) + (swing_side_isopen(2) ? swing_side_pw(2) : 0);
    _sd_ns = swing_side_fit(_sd_sw - FB_GUTTER_W, _sd_sum);   // which show: all when all fit (the render), else the front, the one before it, the rest
    pfx_split = _sd_n >= 2 && _sd_ns >= 2;   // two or more side by side; only the front: the tabs
    _sd_fb0 = fb_open;
    _sd_sum = (side_sh0 ? side_cw0 : 0) + (side_sh1 ? side_cw1 : 0) + (side_sh2 ? side_cw2 : 0);   // the shown ones' widths (squeezed or their own)
    _sd_rest = max(0, (_sd_sw - FB_GUTTER_W) - _sd_sum);   // a dragged width past the panels' own (or the squeeze's rounding): the LAST shown column takes it
    pfx_split ? (
      // side by side: the editor, the sequencer, then the browser with the gutter -- the shown ones, in that order; each
      // takes the presses in its own column from the same stash (the browser's draw first: the slot's ground colours are its)
      _sd_cx = _sd_sx + (side_sh1 ? side_cw1 : 0) + (side_sh2 ? side_cw2 : 0) + (side_sh0 ? 0 : _sd_rest);
      side_sh0 ? swing_fb_draw(_sd_cx, y + _sd_th, x + w - _sd_cx, h - _sd_th)
      : fb_place == 3 ? swing_side_gutter_draw(_sd_cx, y + _sd_th, x + w - _sd_cx, h - _sd_th, 1)
      : swing_side_isopen(0) ? swing_side_fb_blind(_sd_sx, y + _sd_th, _sd_sw, h - _sd_th)   // open but left out (a tab): blind over the whole slot, as under the tabs; the columns paint over its body
                             : swing_side_fb_blind(_sd_cx, y + _sd_th, x + w - _sd_cx, h - _sd_th);   // present and closed: blind (the title row's dim cell opens it)
      _sd_cx = _sd_sx;
      side_sh1 ? ( _sd_cw = side_cw1 + ((!side_sh2 && !side_sh0) ? _sd_rest : 0); swing_pfx_draw(_sd_cx, y + _sd_th, _sd_cw, h - _sd_th); _sd_cx += _sd_cw; );
      side_sh2 ? ( _sd_cw = side_cw2 + (!side_sh0 ? _sd_rest : 0); swing_sseq_draw(_sd_cx, y + _sd_th, _sd_cw, h - _sd_th); _sd_cx += _sd_cw; );
    ) : side_front == 0 ? (
      swing_fb_draw(_sd_sx, y + _sd_th, _sd_sw, h - _sd_th);   // tabs, the browser in front, as ever
    ) : (
      fb_place == 3 ? swing_side_gutter_draw(_sd_sx, y + _sd_th, _sd_sw, h - _sd_th, 1) : swing_side_fb_blind(_sd_sx, y + _sd_th, _sd_sw, h - _sd_th);
      side_front == 1 ? swing_pfx_draw(_sd_sx, y + _sd_th, _sd_sw - FB_GUTTER_W, h - _sd_th)
                      : swing_sseq_draw(_sd_sx, y + _sd_th, _sd_sw - FB_GUTTER_W, h - _sd_th);
    );
    // the handle folds the whole slot: the browser's chevron took the real mouse (fb_open went 0), or the stash's press
    // landed on the gutter (the frame's copies: the rig's fake mouse too)
    // the seam: the slot's width handle, painted over the columns' left edge and read from the stash
    swing_side_seam_draw(x, y, swing_px(FB_SEAM_W), h);
    swing_side_handle(x, y, swing_px(FB_SEAM_W), h, 1);
    _sd_fold = (_sd_fb0 && !fb_open && fb_place != 3) || (_fb_g_lmbdown && mx >= _sd_gx && mx < x + w && my >= y + _sd_th && my < y + h);
    _sd_fold ? ( fx_place != 3 ? pfx_open = 0; seq_place == 1 ? seq_shown = 0; fb_place != 3 ? fb_open = 0; side_front = 0; );
    swing_side_tabs_draw(_sd_sx, y, _sd_sw, _sd_th, pfx_split);
  );
);
